<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Pull the server's backups to this Mac (SESSION-2026-08-29-ISSUES 3.1).

  This is the OFFSITE half of the backup story. scripts/backup.sh runs on the
  Ubuntu server and writes to the same disk it just dumped; this job copies those
  dumps to a second machine, which is the part that makes them survive a drive
  failure.

  NOT INSTALLED BY DEFAULT, and deliberately so. This Mac is a cold standby: its
  whole point is that nothing here starts on its own. Bootstrapping a LaunchAgent
  is a decision to make on purpose, not a side effect of a code change -- the
  migration's hardest-won lesson was that launchd jobs come back unannounced.

  Install (no sudo -- this is a LaunchAgent, not a LaunchDaemon):

    cp scripts/com.praponb.inventory.pull-backups.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) \
      ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.praponb.inventory.pull-backups.plist

  Uninstall:

    launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/com.praponb.inventory.pull-backups
    launchctl disable gui/$(id -u)/com.praponb.inventory.pull-backups

  It needs working key-based ssh to the server as the logged-in user; launchd
  jobs cannot answer a passphrase prompt, so an ssh key with a passphrase that
  is not in the agent will make every run hang or fail.

  RunAtLoad takes one immediately at login, so a Mac that was asleep through its
  slot is not left a full day behind.

  KeepAlive is deliberately absent: this is a periodic task, not a daemon. With
  KeepAlive launchd would restart it the moment it exits and pull in a loop.

  PATH must be set explicitly. launchd gives a job a minimal PATH that does not
  include /opt/homebrew/bin, so the newer rsync is not found.

  BACKUP_MIRROR_DIR puts a second copy in iCloud Drive. It is a mirror, not the
  primary: iCloud here runs with "Optimize Mac Storage", so macOS may evict the
  local copy and leave a placeholder. Recovery must not depend on a download.
  Uncomment it only if that trade-off is acceptable.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>Label</key>
	<string>com.praponb.inventory.pull-backups</string>
	<key>ProgramArguments</key>
	<array>
		<string>/bin/bash</string>
		<string>/Users/praponb/GitHub/Nexus_ClaudeCode/scripts/pull-backups.sh</string>
	</array>
	<key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
	<dict>
		<key>PATH</key>
		<string>/usr/local/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
		<key>BACKUP_PULL_DIR</key>
		<string>/Users/praponb/inventory-backups</string>
		<key>BACKUP_PULL_KEEP</key>
		<string>30</string>
		<!--
		<key>BACKUP_MIRROR_DIR</key>
		<string>/Users/praponb/Library/Mobile Documents/com~apple~CloudDocs/Inventory-Backups</string>
		-->
	</dict>
	<key>RunAtLoad</key>
	<true/>
	<key>StartInterval</key>
	<integer>86400</integer>
	<key>StandardOutPath</key>
	<string>/Users/praponb/Library/Logs/com.praponb.inventory.pull-backups.log</string>
	<key>StandardErrorPath</key>
	<string>/Users/praponb/Library/Logs/com.praponb.inventory.pull-backups.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
